Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(tools): tell a model with no tools that it has none

With no tools in the request, a model answers "run this" or "what tools do you
have" from its training and says it ran the code or made the plot, although
nothing ran. When the turn has no built-in tools and no MCP/extension tools,
append one sentence to the system prompt: it has no tools, so it should give
code or steps for the user instead. It is one sentence because small local
models can have a 4k context.

buildPromptWithToolNote() in the registry now owns the turn's tool line (text
hint, no-tools note, or nothing) for both send and regenerate.

Ported from fl4p/off-grid-ai-mobile 68a62a632 + 56944410f (Fabian).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
